# `moral` (ethics or lesson) is often confused with `morale` (spirit or confidence).
expr verb [boost, boosts, boosted, boosting, bolster, bolsters, bolstered, bolstering, lift, lifts, lifted, lifting, raise, raises, raised, raising, improve, improves, improved, improving, hurt, hurts, hurting, lower, lowers, lowered, lowering, undermine, undermines, undermined, undermining, destroy, destroys, destroyed, destroying, crush, crushes, crushed, crushing, sap, saps, sapped, sapping, shatter, shatters, shattered, shattering]
expr group [team, employee, staff, troop, worker, player, soldier, student, crew, group, office, company, workplace]
expr copula [is, was, has, seems, remains]
expr state [high, low, soaring, plummeting, dropping, sinking, flagging, fading, crumbling, collapsing]
expr main [<(@verb moral ![NOUN, ADJ]), moral>, <(@verb moral.), moral>, <(@group moral ![NOUN, ADJ]), moral>, <(@group moral.), moral>, <([low, high, poor, good, strong] moral [is, was, among, within, across]), moral>, <(moral @copula @state), moral>]

let message "Did you mean `morale`? `Moral` relates to ethics or a lesson; `morale` refers to spirit or confidence."
let description "Corrects `moral` to `morale` when referring to spirit, confidence, or enthusiasm."
let kind "Malapropism"
let becomes "morale"
let strategy "MatchCase"

test "The offsite helped boost moral across the engineering org." "The offsite helped boost morale across the engineering org."
test "Constant delays can hurt moral." "Constant delays can hurt morale."
test "Team moral is high heading into the release." "Team morale is high heading into the release."
test "Employee moral has been dropping all quarter." "Employee morale has been dropping all quarter."
test "With staff moral at a record low, changes were needed." "With staff morale at a record low, changes were needed."
test "High moral among the crew kept the project moving." "High morale among the crew kept the project moving."

allows "The moral of the story is clear."
allows "We should never compromise our moral values."
allows "Public policy cannot ignore moral philosophy."
allows "They refused to lower moral standards for short-term gain."
allows "We discussed moral responsibility during the seminar."
